openclatura structure-to-name source and reference data
======================================================

Historical ReShiki paths below retain the source-repository inventory.
In nazuchem-s2n, src/naming/openclatura/ maps to the crate's src/;
fixture paths refer to the standalone repository root. The root
PROVENANCE-nazuchem.toml ledger identifies the incorporated subset.

src/naming/openclatura/ is a native Rust adaptation of the openclatura 0.4.3
plain-name pipeline, from chains to fused ring systems. Its embedded
data/ JSON registries are copied from the same upstream release. The graph
adapter uses ReShiki's native chemistry implementation in place of RDKit;
tests/fixtures/openclatura/graph_oracle.json records upstream read_smiles
results with RDKit 2026.09.1 for comparison with that adapter.

tests/fixtures/s2n/openclatura_tests.tsv and the openclatura_name column of
tests/fixtures/s2n/bakeoff_corpus.tsv are derived from openclatura 0.4.3
(lamalab-org, https://github.com/lamalab-org/openclatura), commit
90dc5bcb4910c196122ec0405d06a32929a8f308:

- SMILES strings and expected names mined from its tests/ directory;
- names produced by openclatura 0.4.3 for those SMILES and for the bake-off
  corpus, used as the port-parity reference.

