Scope clarification for standalone nazuchem:
src/naming/openclatura/ began as a port of openclatura 0.4.3, extended in
ReShiki. The introductory source description above records that lineage;
the current JSON registries include both copied and locally adapted data,
and source modules also contain separately identified local implementations.
PROVENANCE-nazuchem.toml and Rust source/function headers record those
boundaries, upstream paths and pins. OPSIN-derived data retains its own
source/version statements; not every underlying generation revision is known.

src/naming/openclatura/python_int_set.rs additionally adapts CPython 3.12
Objects/setobject.c under Python-2.0. Its exact patch/commit is unresolved;
see licenses/cpython/LICENSE and licenses/cpython/NOTICE for the complete
licence/history and the source-pin qualification. It is not asserted to be
original code or covered solely by openclatura's MIT grant.

src/data/bluebook/p25_retained.tsv lists the retained heterocycle names of IUPAC
Nomenclature of Organic Chemistry: Recommendations and Preferred Names 2013,
P-25.2.1 Table 2.8, transcribed from https://iupac.qmul.ac.uk/BlueBook/P2.html;
IUPAC holds copyright in the Recommendations. The names are included as factual
data with this attribution; this package's licences do not cover the file, and
no licence is asserted for it (SPDX NOASSERTION).

tests/fixtures/s2n/bakeoff_corpus.tsv is a test fixture kept only in the source
repository and absent from every published package. It contains PubChem compound
IDs and the IUPAC names PubChem lists for them
(https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov); no licence is asserted for it.
